[ti:Somewhere, Sometime]
[ar:Ash Stu]
[al:Ash Stu, Vol. I]
[re:aligned with Demucs vocal separation + MMS forced alignment; edit timestamps by hand if a line is off]
[00:18.52]If I could find the words to say
[00:23.76]And strings to piece a tune
[00:26.38]I'd write a million songs to play
[00:32.87]To make your smile bloom
[00:36.16]If I could box the sun away
[00:41.44]And steal it from the sky
[00:43.78]I'd save it for a rainy day
[00:50.43]To raise your sunken eyes
[01:17.58]I don't care how long it takes
[01:21.32]Or how much breath I'll maybe waste
[01:25.49]I'll search this rock and many more
[01:30.19]We'll meet upon a distant star
[01:34.33]I've dreamt of you, ten thousand times
[01:38.92]But haven't seen your face
[01:41.76]And yet it feels, we've always touched
[01:47.37]Through oddities in time and space
[01:52.49]All I've ever really wanted
[01:56.52]Was you to help me build a rocket
[01:59.88]And blast away
[02:03.52]Far from this place, please
[02:08.28]Blast away with me, towards the stars
[02:16.24]Into the eye, of the man in the moon
[02:27.65]Wave goodbye, and close the capsule door
[02:34.74]We'll watch the world shrink away, as we depart
[03:01.84]If I'm with you I'm fairly certain
[03:07.43]Nothing out there would make me frightened
[03:11.22]I'd only need to hear your voice
[03:16.24]And all my doubts would be destroyed
[03:20.22]So if one day, our fuel runs out
[03:24.42]And we're barreling towards a black hole's mouth
[03:29.17]I'd want to hold your hands in mine
[03:32.18]And count the seconds passing by
[03:37.38]I'd be happy then and there
[03:42.14]Just grateful that I got to share
[03:45.88]A perfect moment, in a perfect life
[03:50.32]With you always by my side
[04:17.82]Somewhere, sometime
[04:22.46]Beyond the sun's shine
[04:26.27]Over the rainbow
[04:31.61]Under three moon's glow
[04:35.32]You're staring at the sky
[04:39.65]Waiting for my flashing lights
[04:44.16]To descend, from the stars
[04:48.77]And then at last, we're not apart
[05:10.09]Would I know the words to say
[05:13.59]Could I find the notes to play
[05:18.61]To ask you would you join my trek
[05:23.34]Throughout the universe and back
